lers' lineup roughly in mid-November.","player":8482221.0,"return":"2026-11-09","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"EDM"},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Alec Regula","note":"Regula continues to work his way back from offseason surgery that caused him to miss the entire preseason. With the shift to LTIR, the 26-year-old defenseman can be expected to miss at least the next nine games, having already been out of action for one, though it could be longer, considering the team hasn't provided a specific update.","player":8480831.0,"return":"2026-11-21","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"EDM"},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Matt Savoie","note":"By moving Savoie to LTIR, the Oilers will get some cap relief while he is sidelined, as their injuries have started to pile up. The 22-year-old forward logged all 82 regular-season games in his rookie campaign, generating 18 goals and 19 assists, including seven power-play points. Considering Savoie is expected to miss at least the first two weeks of the season, fantasy managers probably shouldn't be expecting him to significantly outperform those numbers in 2026-27.","player":8483512.0,"return":"2026-11-24","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"EDM"},{"date":"2026-09-29","name":"Frederik Andersen","note":"Andersen, who signed a one-year, $1 million contract with Edmonton in July, is still rehabbing from a knee injury. He posted a 16-14-5 record with a 3.05 GAA and an .874 save percentage in 35 appearances for Carolina during the 2025-26 regular season. Once he's ready to play in the 2026-27 campaign with the Oilers, Andersen could compete for starts with Tristan Jarry and Devon Levi.","player":8475883.0,"return":"2026-12-30","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"EDM"},{"date":"2026-09-29","name":"Mattias Janmark","note":"Janmark underwent an undisclosed procedure earlier in the year, but he's currently shelved until further notice. The 33-year-old winger was limited in 2025-26, where he compiled a goal and eight points across 43 regular-season outings. In his absence, Mathieu Joseph and Max Jones are expected to serve as the team's left wingers in the bottom six to open the 2026-27 campaign.","player":8477406.0,"return":"2026-11-28","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"EDM"},{"date":"2026-09-29","name":"Atro Leppanen","note":"ir-nr","player":NaN,"return":"2026-11-28","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"EDM"},{"date":"2026-11-01","name":"Ryan Pulock","note":"out","player":8477506.0,"return":"2026-11-28","src":"ESPN","status":"Out","team":"NYI"},{"date":"2026-10-26","name":"Matias Maccelli","note":"After suffering a lower-body injury against Toronto on Oct. 17, Maccelli has sat out the last three games. He was expected to miss 2-4 weeks, so his move to the IR list won't impact his timeline. Maccelli has earned two goals, six points and 13 shots on net in eight appearances this season.","player":8481711.0,"return":"2026-11-17","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"NYI"},{"date":"2026-10-26","name":"Calum Ritchie","note":"ir","player":8484221.0,"return":"2026-12-01","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"NYI"},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Alexander Romanov","note":"ir","player":8481014.0,"return":"2027-04-08","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"NYI"},{"date":"2026-10-15","name":"Mathew Barzal","note":"Barzal racked up 72 points in 81 regular-season games last year, including 20 power-play points and four game-winning goals. At this point, the team hasn't offered any specific recovery timeline for the 29-year-old center. Whenever Barzal returns, it should be in a top-six role that includes time with the man advantage.","player":8478445.0,"return":"2026-11-07","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"NYI"},{"date":"2026-08-26","name":"Frederik Andersen","note":"Knee: The Oilers announced on Tuesday (Sept. 29) that Andersen is not expected to be back until maybe December.","player":8475883.0,"retur